cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use MOSAIC RESCUE, or reuse its methods, please cite it as below.
title: "MOSAIC RESCUE: a falsification-first analysis of one paediatric genome with suspected mosaic variegated aneuploidy"
abstract: >-
  Research-first genomic analysis of a single paediatric patient with suspected
  mosaic variegated aneuploidy, produced for the Rare Disease, Real Kid: MVA
  Hackathon 2026. Track 1 establishes a causal hypothesis through a panel-free
  genome-wide search and ACMG-style curation of both alleles, reporting the
  frozen preregistered ranking alongside a later sensitivity analysis. Track 2
  decomposes the therapeutic chain into eight evidence bridges audited across
  ten dimensions, and stops at a falsifiable preclinical experiment rather than
  a drug recommendation. Also reports a preregistered simulation in which a
  site-wise unphased B-allele-frequency baseline loses power as a variegated
  aneuploidy event grows, because contributions from different lineages cancel.
  That baseline is not MoChA, the result is simulated rather than observed in
  patient data, and no superiority over a phased method is claimed.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Manuel
    family-names: Mancebo
    alias: Manceb0
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-02"
# Code is DUAL-licensed, MIT OR CC-BY-4.0 (LICENSE); documentation, notebooks
# and figures are CC BY 4.0 (LICENSE-DOCS).
#
# Why both: the hackathon rules place submissions, code included, under CC BY,
# so MIT alone would not comply. Creative Commons in turn advises against CC
# licences for software. Offering both satisfies each requirement without
# weakening either, and the recipient chooses.
#
# CFF takes a single SPDX identifier per entry, so the two are listed.
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Manceb0/mosaic-rescue"
keywords:
  - mosaic variegated aneuploidy
  - BUB1B
  - rare disease
  - whole genome sequencing
  - variant prioritization
  - ACMG curation
  - drug repurposing
  - chromosomal instability
  - falsifiability
references:
  - type: data
    title: "Rare Disease, Real Kid: MVA Hackathon 2026 patient dataset"
    notes: >-
      Not redistributed. Not included in this repository. Provided under the
      terms of the challenge; the family consented to their story being shared.
